	(text "MAIN BUS BREAKER - TPS48111-Q1 smart high-side driver between the battery (VBAT_IN, J1) and the motor bus (VBUS)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 20 0)
		(effects (font (size 3 3) (bold yes)) (justify left bottom))
		(uuid "c9a7944a-5cb2-5711-910c-c6c02718dd8d")
	)
	(text "Back-to-back Q801/Q802 (common source): bidirectional when on (regen reaches the battery), blocks both ways when off. Logic supply (F1) taps VBAT_IN before the breaker, so the STM32 and brakes stay powered when the bus trips."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 28 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.6 1.6)) (justify left bottom))
		(uuid "108ba7c3-3119-573b-9dd1-b14567434061")
	)
	(text "Protection (TPS4811 SLUSEE5E eq. 6/7/9/11/13): RSNS 0.5 mOhm, RSET 100 R. IOC = 80 A (R815 30.1k, blank tOC = 5 ms with C804 330 nF, auto-retry ~7.5 s). ISC = 150 A (R816 4.32k, trips in 1.2 us). IMON gain 61.2 (R813 6.8k): 30.6 mV/A -> 1.84 V at 60 A."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 33 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.6 1.6)) (justify left bottom))
		(uuid "35d9799c-8754-54a7-9c14-7a6fb16db149")
	)
	(text "UVLO (EN/UVLO 1.18 V rising / 1.11 V falling): R806 300k / R807 12k = /26: ON at 30.7 V (3.07 V/cell), OFF at 28.9 V (2.89 V/cell). Faults FLT_I/FLT_T open drain -> BUS_FLT_N -> STM32 PD8; BUS_IMON -> 74HC4051 U706 ch5 (ESC_MCU)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 38 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.6 1.6)) (justify left bottom))
		(uuid "eac16931-3d84-5447-ad02-d982dfdd1385")
	)
	(text "NOTE: VS/CS+/ISCP are rated -1 V: a reversed battery still damages U801, but Q801/Q802 keep reverse voltage off the ESC side. Keep the external 80 A fuse."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 43 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.6 1.6)) (justify left bottom))
		(uuid "3280afa6-5a6d-5c9f-bd18-a4a9eb0d13f7")
	)
	(text "AUTONOMOUS ENABLE + PRECHARGE (no MCU). U802 LM339 on +5V, open-collector outputs pulled up to +3V3. Inputs stay inside the 0..3.5 V common-mode range up to VBUS = 60 V."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 214 0)
		(effects (font (size 2 2) (bold yes)) (justify left bottom))
		(uuid "4dac4828-51cf-5c41-8be6-5e9de4f66e4b")
	)
	(text "A (OUT1) BUS_GOOD_N: low when VBUS > 92 % of VBAT_IN (R819/R820 vs R821/R822). Q804 inverts it: BUS_EN (INP, main FETs) is high only while the bus is good. Sticky: R823 from BUS_EN lifts VBUS_DIV, so A releases only below ~40-53 % (VBUS 12 V at 30 V, 22 V at 42 V)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 220 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left bottom))
		(uuid "bb37d64b-0ba8-5f53-98bc-f9d60f5c8fb1")
	)
	(text "PRECHG_EN (INP_G, precharge FET Q803) = high while the bus is NOT good, pulled low via D801 when it is good, or by B (OUT2) after the timeout."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 224.5 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left bottom))
		(uuid "bff3f33c-f11e-5b7d-b2b9-9cbb0132a96a")
	)
	(text "Timeout PRE_TMR: R827 220k / C809 2.2 uF from +3V3 to SEQ_REF 1.03 V (R828 22k / R829 10k): 0.18 s = R C ln(3.3 / 2.27). Reset (held low) while the bus is good (D801) or while VBAT_IN < 26.8 V (C, OUT3: BUS_UVLO < SEQ_REF, below the TPS falling threshold)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 229 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left bottom))
		(uuid "fb259d41-3025-58c2-aba7-e1f5b2a23340")
	)
	(text "Sequence: +3V3 up, VBAT >= 30.7 V -> INP_G high (precharge through R803/R804 20 R, tau ~20 ms with ~1 mF) -> VBUS reaches 92 % (~60 ms incl. BST charge) -> INP high (main on), INP_G low."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 233.5 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left bottom))
		(uuid "02b415fd-e257-58e7-bd97-03ef64bafc34")
	)
	(text "Faults: OC/SC trip -> VBUS collapses below the sticky threshold -> INP low (resets the TPS fault counter), precharge retried once for 0.18 s; a short keeps VBUS low -> timeout -> precharge stays off (latched) until the pack is reconnected. VBAT sag < UVLO: TPS off; recovers by itself if VBAT returns >= 30.7 V."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 238 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left bottom))
		(uuid "8a163209-22f2-5341-acfc-5811b974c42d")
	)
	(text "CHECK: R803/R804 must take one 0.18 s pulse into a shorted bus (42 V / 20 R = 2.1 A, 88 W total, ~16 J). Unused comparator D: IN4+ = GND, IN4- = SEQ_REF, OUT4 open."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 242.5 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left bottom))
		(uuid "9f355a5f-7d86-588f-9edc-afda21a8e6a9")
	)
